WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.988
- Looking to the future years

00:00:00.988 --> 00:00:03.540
you've been open about not wanting kids.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:04.772
So is this still a thing?
- Yes.

00:00:04.772 --> 00:00:05.605
- Okay.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.438
You say hard yes.

00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:07.565
- I still don't want kids, yeah.

00:00:07.565 --> 00:00:08.730
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.563
- Why?

00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:10.590
Like you just never saw yourself as a dad

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.240
or you just like your time?

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.000
- It doesn't seem that fun.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.060
(audience laughing)

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.730
- I can see how it seems that way.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.563
- Yeah.

00:00:18.563 --> 00:00:20.940
It really does not, it doesn't seem fun.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.610
And most of my friends who
are parents, God bless them,

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.890
spend a lot of their time talking about

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.843
how much they don't like having kids.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.740
And what me and my wife spend
a lot of time talking about

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.360
is how much fun stuff we can do

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.467
because we don't have kids.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.380
- I think that that's
actually pretty rad though

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.600
because I never wanted kids.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.570
Like whenever before I met
my ex and then he had kids,

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.010
and I was like, oh, this is kind of cool.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:44.843
- Yeah.

00:00:44.843 --> 00:00:45.953
- I was like, and I got
to kind of experience it.

00:00:45.953 --> 00:00:47.303
- Yeah, that seems like
a good version of it.

00:00:47.303 --> 00:00:49.440
- So then I ended up having kids because

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.690
and then, so I would, I wouldn't say

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.630
it's like the most fun job
'cause it's like overwhelming.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.463
- [Seth] Yeah.

00:00:55.463 --> 00:00:56.296
- But it's a beautiful thing

00:00:56.296 --> 00:00:58.920
and it's like nothing cooler for me.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.930
But I will say though,
I think it's important

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.730
because people always used
to pressure me about it.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:03.563
- [Seth] Yeah.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.010
- About marriage and about
having kids and like,

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:05.910
it's like not everybody,

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.583
that's not everybody's
dream is to do that.

00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:08.790
- No, and a lot of people I think-

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.230
- I just think it's
important you say that.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.217
- Yeah, a lot of people have kids

00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:12.550
and they don't even think about it.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.383
- Oh my God.

00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:14.860
We call those people
that have accessories.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:16.140
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.885
Or they just think that's
the next thing you do in life

00:01:17.885 --> 00:01:19.530
is you have kids and then they look back

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.180
and they were like, "I
didn't have to have kids?"

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.020
- No.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.040
My friend was like that's a person

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.810
that has a kid as an accessory.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:25.710
And I'm like, that's not,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.290
that's a lot of therapy in the waiting.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.620
But anyway.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.520
- Yeah, but you don't need kids.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.870
There's so many kids.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:31.703
- I know.

00:01:31.703 --> 00:01:32.536
And that's the thing too.

00:01:32.536 --> 00:01:34.027
Yeah.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.610
- Who looks at all the kids out there

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.069
and thinks, "I wish they were more kids."

00:01:37.069 --> 00:01:38.760
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.100
- I guess anybody that wants kids.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.060
- Yeah, not me.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:42.930
- I think that's cool.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.370
And your wife is the same way, right?

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.715
- She does not want kids, no.

00:01:45.715 --> 00:01:46.548
- Yeah.

00:01:46.548 --> 00:01:47.760
- We get a lot of, I don't know.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.430
I know people describe having kids, yeah,

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:53.790
as like brief glimmering moments of beauty

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.740
amongst a sea of pain.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.245
It kind of, whereas not having kids

00:01:58.245 --> 00:02:01.765
it's just lovely all the time.

00:02:01.765 --> 00:02:03.810
There's none of that.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.700
It's just great all day.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.220
I'm never like, "I wish I had kids

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.440
and I'm missing something
by not having them."

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.240
I'm more am doing stuff all the time

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.890
where I look over at my
wife and she looks at me

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.860
and we're like, "If we had
kids, we couldn't do this."

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:17.693
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:17.693 --> 00:02:19.170
- This wouldn't even
remotely be on the table.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:20.003
- No, that's why--

00:02:20.003 --> 00:02:21.257
- We couldn't do any of
this stuff if we had kids.

00:02:21.257 --> 00:02:22.890
- People with kids, that's
what we call me time.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:23.750
- Oh yeah.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:24.583
- You have to carve it out.

00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:25.416
- All the time is me.

00:02:25.416 --> 00:02:28.021
Why would I, who, why
wouldn't it be me time?

00:02:28.021 --> 00:02:28.854
Who, what?

00:02:28.854 --> 00:02:29.850
It's us time.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.905
We do it together, we
wanna spend time together.

00:02:31.905 --> 00:02:33.120
- I think that's really awesome

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.320
and I think it's so cool.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.153
- [Seth] Yeah.

00:02:35.153 --> 00:02:36.150
- To not pressure people and enjoy.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.100
- No, I think there should be more voices

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.989
of that you don't need to have kids.

00:02:39.989 --> 00:02:40.822
- Reason?
- Yeah.

00:02:40.822 --> 00:02:41.655
You don't need to have kids.

00:02:41.655 --> 00:02:44.005
Also, like, won't the world
not be here in 30 years?

00:02:44.005 --> 00:02:45.840
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.003
- Aren't we all gonna die?

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.403
Oh my god.

00:02:49.403 --> 00:02:51.030
Well, I do love my children.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.050
- They seem great.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:52.920
- They're great.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:53.753
- They seem lovely.

00:02:53.753 --> 00:02:55.050
- I'll call you for babysitting.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.340
- Exactly.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.531
- You and your wife would love it.

00:02:57.531 --> 00:02:58.364
- We babysit.

00:02:58.364 --> 00:02:59.197
Yeah, we hang out.

00:02:59.197 --> 00:03:01.770
I love my friend's children
probably than they do

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:03.151
it seems some of the time.

00:03:03.151 --> 00:03:05.190
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.363
- You get to play with 'em, hand 'em back.

00:03:06.363 --> 00:03:07.196
It's the best.

00:03:07.196 --> 00:03:09.460
It's like a grandparent or
an aunt or an uncle, yeah.

